    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0608" n="594" xml:id="pg594"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.6352/9–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-05T11:00:00-04:00">September 5,
                            1945—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>921. Dept’s A–294, August 28.<anchor n="78" xml:id="d458-f1"/> Nothing has come
                    to Embassy’s attention bearing out statement that adequate steps taken for
                    protection security American citizens. On contrary reports from Quechisla–Oploca
                    area situation worse and strike entailing danger to Americans certain before
                    year’s end. Embassy asking American company managers to report carefully what
                    steps taken to protect and whether situation improved. Their reaction will be
                    forwarded Dept. but above submitted for its consideration in tin
                    negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
